### ========================================
### ERROR TEST CASES
### ========================================

### Test Invalid Customer ID (Create)
POST https://localhost:5001/api/customerpolicies
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": -1,
  "policyId": 1,
  "status": "Active",
  "premiumAmount": 5000.00,
  "isActive": true
}

### Expected Response: 400 Bad Request - "Invalid customer ID"

###

### Test Invalid Policy ID (Create)
POST https://localhost:5001/api/customerpolicies
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": 1,
  "policyId": 0,
  "status": "Active",
  "premiumAmount": 5000.00,
  "isActive": true
}

### Expected Response: 400 Bad Request - "Invalid policy ID"

###

### Test Negative Premium Amount (Create)
POST https://localhost:5001/api/customerpolicies
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": 1,
  "policyId": 1,
  "status": "Active",
  "premiumAmount": -1000.00,
  "isActive": true
}

### Expected Response: 400 Bad Request - "Premium amount cannot be negative"

###

### Test Non-existent Policy ID (Get)
GET https://localhost:5001/api/customerpolicies/9999
Accept: application/json

### Expected Response: 404 Not Found - "Customer policy not found"

###

### Test Non-existent Customer ID (Get by Customer)
GET https://localhost:5001/api/customerpolicies/customer/9999
Accept: application/json

### Expected Response: 404 Not Found - "No policies found for this customer"

###

### Test Invalid Customer ID in Get (negative)
GET https://localhost:5001/api/customerpolicies/customer/-1
Accept: application/json

### Expected Response: 400 Bad Request - "Invalid customer ID"

###

### Test Delete Non-existent Policy
DELETE https://localhost:5001/api/customerpolicies/9999
Accept: application/json

### Expected Response: 404 Not Found - "Customer policy not found"

###

### ========================================
### SAMPLE DATA SCENARIOS
### ========================================

### Scenario 1: New Customer Onboarding
### Step 1: Create Policy 1 (Life Insurance - Monthly)
POST https://localhost:5001/api/customerpolicies
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": 3,
  "policyId": 1,
  "purchaseDate": "2025-01-20",
  "expiryDate": "2026-01-20",
  "status": "Active",
  "premiumAmount": 5000.00,
  "paymentFrequency": "Monthly",
  "nextPaymentDueDate": "2025-02-20",
  "remarks": "New customer - Life Insurance enrollment",
  "isActive": true
}

###

### Scenario 1: Step 2 - Create Policy 2 (Health Insurance - Quarterly)
POST https://localhost:5001/api/customerpolicies
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": 3,
  "policyId": 2,
  "purchaseDate": "2025-01-20",
  "expiryDate": "2026-01-20",
  "status": "Pending",
  "premiumAmount": 8000.00,
  "paymentFrequency": "Quarterly",
  "nextPaymentDueDate": "2025-04-20",
  "remarks": "New customer - Health Insurance pending activation",
  "isActive": true
}

###

### Scenario 1: Step 3 - Get All Policies for Customer 3
GET https://localhost:5001/api/customerpolicies/customer/3
Accept: application/json

###

### Scenario 2: Payment Processing
### Step 1 - Record Monthly Payment
PUT https://localhost:5001/api/customerpolicies/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": 1,
  "policyId": 1,
  "purchaseDate": "2024-01-15",
  "expiryDate": "2025-01-15",
  "status": "Active",
  "premiumAmount": 5000.00,
  "paymentFrequency": "Monthly",
  "lastPaymentDate": "2025-01-20",
  "nextPaymentDueDate": "2025-02-20",
  "remarks": "Monthly premium payment received - INR 5000",
  "isActive": true
}

###

### Scenario 2: Step 2 - View Updated Policy
GET https://localhost:5001/api/customerpolicies/1
Accept: application/json

###

### Scenario 3: Policy Renewal
### Step 1 - Get Current Policy Info
GET https://localhost:5001/api/customerpolicies/1
Accept: application/json

###

### Scenario 3: Step 2 - Renew Policy
POST https://localhost:5001/api/customerpolicies/1/renew
Accept: application/json

###

### Scenario 3: Step 3 - Verify Renewal
GET https://localhost:5001/api/customerpolicies/1
Accept: application/json

###

### Scenario 4: Policy Status Tracking
### Step 1 - Get Active Policies
GET https://localhost:5001/api/customerpolicies/customer/1/status/Active
Accept: application/json

###

### Scenario 4: Step 2 - Get Inactive Policies
GET https://localhost:5001/api/customerpolicies/customer/1/status/Inactive
Accept: application/json

###

### Scenario 4: Step 3 - Get Expired Policies
GET https://localhost:5001/api/customerpolicies/customer/1/status/Expired
Accept: application/json

###

### Notes:
### 1. Replace localhost:5001 with your actual API URL and port
### 2. Add Authorization header if API requires authentication:
###    Authorization: Bearer {your-jwt-token}
### 3. Modify CustomerId, PolicyId based on your database
### 4. All dates should be in ISO 8601 format (YYYY-MM-DD)
### 5. PremiumAmount should be positive decimal values
### 6. Valid Status values: Active, Inactive, Expired, Cancelled, Pending
### 7. Valid PaymentFrequency: Monthly, Quarterly, Semi-Annually, Annually
